* TIMES.jl crafted case demo12_xbnd (reference/crafted.toml, 14 Nov 2026): limits on the total
* exchange of a commodity of a region (IRE_XBND), the equations EQ(l)_XBND (eqxbnd.mod L17-56).
* Added to TIMES_Demo demo12 (etsap-TIMES/TIMES_Demo @ 962db86, CC BY 4.0). The regions: REG1
* and REG2 (internal), IMPEXP and MINRNW (external). REG1 and REG2 trade electricity both ways
* (TB_ELC_REG1_REG2_01, at DAYNITE) and gas from REG2 to REG1 (TU_GAS_REG2_REG1_01, at ANNUAL).
* The timeslices: ANNUAL; the seasons S and W; SD, SN (in S) and WD, WN (in W). A record reads
* IRE_XBND(region, year, commodity, timeslice, IMP or EXP, LO/FX/UP).
* New data beside the bounds:
* - IMPELC2, a second electricity import of REG1 from IMPEXP that runs at SEASON, so that a bound
*   at a DAYNITE timeslice is finer than one of its flows (eqxbnd.mod L30: RS_FR).
* - IRE_TSCVT of REG1's season W to a timeslice W of the external region IMPEXP, 0.9: a bound of
*   an external region takes the flows of the internal regions through IRE_TSCVT (L42, L48);
*   by default an external region has the timeslice ANNUAL only (ppmain.mod L967-978).
* The bounds of an internal region (L23-32: all exchange processes of the region with the
* commodity in that direction, whatever the partner):
* - REG1 ELC, IMP, ANNUAL, UP 500 in 2020: every electricity import of REG1 over the year.
* - REG1 ELC, IMP, WD, LO 30 in 2020: the flows at WD in full, the flow of the season W and the
*   flow at ANNUAL with the share of WD; it forces imports.
* - REG1 ELC, EXP, season S, UP 100 in 2030: a bound above the flows' level.
* - REG2 GAS, EXP, ANNUAL, LO 10 in 2020: the export to IMPEXP and the gas link to REG1.
* - REG2 ELC, EXP, ANNUAL, FX 40 in 2020: an equality.
* - REG1 GAS, IMP, WD, UP 5000 in 2030: finer than the commodity's level (GAS is tracked at
*   ANNUAL): the equation has no condition on the commodity's timeslices and the bound is not
*   added up; the flows at ANNUAL count with the share of WD.
* - REG1 COA, EXP, ANNUAL, UP 600 in 2020 with interpolation and forward extrapolation
*   (option 5): rows in 2020, 2030 and 2050.
* - REG2 ELC, IMP, SN, FX with the value EPS in 2020: a row with the right-hand side zero.
* - REG2 ELC, IMP, WN, LO with the value EPS and WD, UP INF, in 2030: no row (eqmain.mod L241
*   and L243).
* - REG1 TOTCO2, IMP, ANNUAL, UP 5 in 2020: no exchange process has the commodity: no row.
* The bounds of an external region (L39-51: the flows of the internal regions in the other
* direction, through the processes linked to the external region):
* - IMPEXP GAS, IMP, ANNUAL, LO 3 in 2020: the gas exports of REG1 and REG2 to IMPEXP.
* - IMPEXP ELC, EXP, ANNUAL, UP 300 in 2020: the electricity imports of REG1 and REG2 from
*   IMPEXP.
* - MINRNW COA, EXP, ANNUAL, UP 9000 in 2020 with option 5: the coal mining of both regions,
*   in 2020, 2030 and 2050.
* - IMPEXP COA, IMP, ANNUAL, FX with the value EPS in 2030: a row with the right-hand side zero.
* - IMPEXP ELC, EXP, W, UP 150 in 2030: REG1's imports from IMPEXP in the season W, times the
*   IRE_TSCVT of 0.9 (REG2 has no IRE_TSCVT to W of IMPEXP and is not in the row).
* - IMPEXP ELC, EXP, WD, UP 50 in 2020: no IRE_TSCVT to WD of IMPEXP: a row without a variable.
* - MINRNW ELC, EXP, ANNUAL, UP 50 in 2020: MINRNW has no electricity link: no row.
$ONEMPTY
$ONEPS
$ONWARNING
SET PRC /
IMPELC2
/
SET PRC_MAP /
REG1.IRE.IMPELC2
/
SET PRC_TSL /
REG1.IMPELC2.SEASON
/
SET PRC_ACTUNT /
REG1.IMPELC2.ELC.PJ
/
SET TOP /
REG1.IMPELC2.ELC.OUT
/
SET TOP_IRE /
IMPEXP.ELC.REG1.ELC.IMPELC2
/
SET PRC_DESC /
REG1.IMPELC2 'Import of Electricity Step 2 (by season)'
/
PARAMETER
ACT_BND ' '/
REG1.0.IMPELC2.ANNUAL.UP 5
REG1.2005.IMPELC2.ANNUAL.UP 200
/
PARAMETER
IRE_PRICE ' '/
REG1.2005.IMPELC2.ELC.ANNUAL.REG1.IMP.MEURO05 5.3
/
PARAMETER
IRE_TSCVT ' '/
REG1.W.IMPEXP.W 0.9
/
PARAMETER
IRE_XBND ' '/
REG1.2020.ELC.ANNUAL.IMP.UP 500
REG1.2020.ELC.WD.IMP.LO 30
REG1.2030.ELC.S.EXP.UP 100
REG2.2020.GAS.ANNUAL.EXP.LO 10
REG2.2020.ELC.ANNUAL.EXP.FX 40
REG1.2030.GAS.WD.IMP.UP 5000
REG1.0.COA.ANNUAL.EXP.UP 5
REG1.2020.COA.ANNUAL.EXP.UP 600
REG2.2020.ELC.SN.IMP.FX EPS
REG2.2030.ELC.WN.IMP.LO EPS
REG2.2030.ELC.WD.IMP.UP INF
REG1.2020.TOTCO2.ANNUAL.IMP.UP 5
IMPEXP.2020.GAS.ANNUAL.IMP.LO 3
IMPEXP.2020.ELC.ANNUAL.EXP.UP 300
MINRNW.0.COA.ANNUAL.EXP.UP 5
MINRNW.2020.COA.ANNUAL.EXP.UP 9000
IMPEXP.2030.COA.ANNUAL.IMP.FX EPS
IMPEXP.2030.ELC.W.EXP.UP 150
IMPEXP.2020.ELC.WD.EXP.UP 50
MINRNW.2020.ELC.ANNUAL.EXP.UP 50
/
